  "diagnostic_summary": [
    "This first 4-paper holdout has 4/16 strict complete-and-supported deliveries, distinct from 135/135 supported published atoms; fact support does not imply completeness.",
    "Published prose meets the complete semantic rubric in 7/16 answerable questions. Three of these remain partial_answer in the application, so the frozen strict delivery metric stays 4/16. The original SC paper review used semantic-completeness wording; the combined report explicitly resolves that naming difference without overwriting it.",
    "One answerable refusal is associated with incomplete actual retrieval. The remaining answerable retrieval sets collectively support the frozen criteria, including the three failed tasks; answer/condition omissions, semantic checker disagreements and infrastructure failures therefore require separate reporting.",
    "All three engineering failures are model_timeout; they remain selected failures without reruns, and no unissued candidate answer is scored as published.",
    "Four intentionally unanswerable questions appropriately withhold unsupported requested values with a current-retrieval-scoped message; no unsupported substantive answer was published on those questions.",
    "The four table/footnote probes remain in the main denominator: one strict complete delivery, two partial deliveries and one refusal. Table columns, splits, conditions and omissions are assessed under the original frozen rubric.",
    "Known usage is only a subtotal: three timed-out calls lack token usage, and all 58 calls have unknown cost. USD 0 known subtotal is not zero total cost.",
    "No application/prompt/retrieval changes, model retries or replacement labels were made from these held-out results. The root receives only final metrics and failure classes, not per-paper reference-answer details for tuning. This is an AI-prepared candidate holdout; human labels and product/learning acceptance are pending and pretraining exposure cannot be excluded."
  ],
